This program is a simulation to see the effects of multi-headed attention has on training time as more heads are introduced. In order for this to be done, a dataset is generated to be used for training and then information is kept track of like the effects that more heads has on forward pass time, overall training time, and the effect of loss over time. In order to keep everything consistent the only thing that changes is the number of heads of attention that is being done. Perameters such as epochs, data size, etc... are kept the same. From the findings, it is found that the increase between training time and forward pass time is linear on average. In contrast, the loss over time changes quite drastically depending on the number of heads of attention with there being less loss over time the more heads there are. This program can be ran through either cpu or gpu to make it more dynamic with testing, though saddly I did not have any gpus at the time to use in parallel. The png files of the results can be found within this file.